# Kod 9928 — PYNQ GPS baseline

When the user says **9928**, they refer to this **stable working setup**. Preserve it; do not break auto-boot or the PC-only deploy workflow.

## Hardware

- Board: **TUL PYNQ-Z2** @ `192.168.2.99`, SSH `xilinx` / `xilinx`
- GPS: **u-blox NEO-6M** (GY-NEO6MV2), 9600 baud NMEA
- Wiring (RPi header): VCC→Pin **1**, GND→Pin **6**, GPS TX→Pin **10**, GPS RX→Pin **8**
- Bitstream: `gps_uart.bin` (AXI UART Lite @ `0x42C00000`)

## Software (do not require SD card reflash for updates)

- **PC deploy:** run `9928.bat` or `deploy_gps.bat` from repo root (`C:\Users\oalpe\Desktop\neo_gps`)
- Uploads `gps_web.py`, `neo_gps_pynq.py`, `gps_uart.bin` via SSH/SCP
- Installs **systemd** `neo-gps.service` — GPS web starts automatically on every boot
- Dashboard: **http://192.168.2.99:8080** (map + NMEA tab GGA/RMC/GSA/GSV/VTG/GLL)

## Rules

- Run **only one** GPS process (`gps_web.py` OR `neo_gps_pynq.py`) — two clients → bus error
- Software updates = PC deploy (`9928.bat`), **not** SD card image changes
- Showcase repo: https://github.com/Alp2246/pynq-z2-gps-nmea

## On "9928" request

Use/deploy this baseline; run or suggest `9928.bat`; keep systemd auto-start enabled.

**Mutual exclusion:** Sensor panel is **9930** (`sensor_panel/9930.bat`) — same UART, cannot run with 9928 simultaneously.
